+**Construct validity: the assumptions of the reference-only certificate.** From references alone no precision order and no slope sign can be certified without an assumption on how often present objects are named (Supplementary S11.3), so every reference-only verdict is conditional on the floor (F$_w$) and on (A0), (A1) and (A1+). The floor cannot be checked from the references: the present objects that writers rarely name are exactly the part the references leave unknown, and the primary floor $w_0 = 0.20$ was fixed from an earlier calculation, not derived. (A1) is a modelling assumption on XM3600-600, on COCO-5000 and on the released image sets of Part P and is not checked (the diagnostic of Section 5 checks reference order only). (A0) fails wherever a reference names a class absent from the image (Section 4.2); the instance-only rows of Part V and the count printed beside H3 show how often this happens on the sets where it can be counted. (A1+) is dropped by the secondary Hoeffding budget. The derivation of the budget (Supplementary S11.2) has had no external proof review.
